
## Article

```catala
declaration scope A:
  input dur content duration
  output o content duration

scope A:
    definition o equals dur + 1 year

declaration scope B:
    output o content duration

scope B:
    definition o equals (output of A with {-- dur : 1 month}).o
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala DCalc -s A
let scope A (A_in: A_in): A =
  let get dur : duration = A_in.dur_in in
  let set o : duration =
    error_empty ⟨ ⟨true ⊢ ⟨dur + [1 years, 0 months, 0 days]⟩⟩ | false ⊢ ∅ ⟩
  in
  return { A o = o; }
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Interpret -s B
┌─[RESULT]─ B ─
│ o = [1 year, 1 month]
└─
```

For now the concolic interpreter refuses to handle durations that are not just
a number of days.

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Concolic --conc-optim=incremental -s A
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  [DateEncoding] Duration literals containing years or months not supported
│
└─
#return code 123#
```
